ellow structures more clearly:\n- Left yellow: cols 16-27, with a gap at cols 20-23 (rows 52-55)\n- Right yellow: cols 40-51, with a gap at cols 44-47 (rows 52-55)\nThe yellow structures are like \"U\" shapes with openings at the top center. The openings are 4 cols wide (cols 20-23 for left, cols 44-47 for right).\nThe blue block is 4x20. It's too wide to fit into the 4-col openings.\nBut wait, the adjacency list shows:\n- [2, 6] and [2, 7]: orange background is adjacent to both yellow structures\n- [6, 8]: left yellow is adjacent to light gray bar\n- [7, 8]: right yellow is adjacent to light gray bar\nSo the yellow structures are sitting on the light gray bar at the bottom.\nLet me think about what the goal could be. The blue block is 4x20. The yellow structures have 4-col openings. Maybe the goal is to position the blue block so that it's above one of the openings, and then drop it down.\nBut the blue block is 20 cols wide, and the openings are only 4 cols wide. So the blue block can't fit through the openings.\nUnless... the blue block can be resized or split. Let me check if there's a way to change the blue block's size.\nActually, let me try a completely different approach. Maybe the goal is to move the blue block to a position where it touches the magenta block. The magenta block is at rows 4-7, cols 36-39. The blue block is at rows 12-15, cols 28-47. The blue block is below the magenta block, with a gap of rows 8-11 between them.\nSince the blue block can't move up further, maybe I need to move it horizontally to be adjacent to the magenta block. The magenta block is at cols 36-39, and the blue block is at cols 28-47. So the blue block already overlaps horizontally with the magenta block.\nWait, maybe the goal is to have the blue block touch the magenta block from the side. The magenta block is at cols 36-39. To touch it from the left, the blue block should end at col 35. To touch it from the right, the blue block should start at col 40.\nCurrently the blue b